[[File:Greymane Wall Open.png|thumb|350px|The Greymane Wall in ''World of Warcraft''.]]
[[File:Greymane Wall-Gilneas.png|thumb|350px|The Greymane Wall, Gilneas side.]]
'''The Greymane Wall''', also referred to as the '''Greymane Gate''',<ref>{{questlong|Neutral|39|Legend of Dawnstone}}</ref> was erected after the Second War by [[Genn Greymane]], as the nation of [[Gilneas (kingdom)|Gilneas]] isolated itself from the [[Alliance]] due to a dispute surrounding the internment camps for the orcs. It is a large wall with a portcullis, located at the southern edge of the [[Silverpine Forest]] (near [[Pyrewood Village]]) and the northern edge of [[Gilneas]].

The Greymane Wall is the only evident site of Gilneas. This enormous gray wall marks the boundary between Gilneas and Lordaeron. No guards stand at its battlements or man its gates — the wall seems dead. Nevertheless, refugees from the north camp in the wall’s shadow, hoping for succor. These unfortunates never saw a Gilnean and are easy prey for the worgen that occasionally stray this far south from Shadowfang Keep.

Those on the other side in Gilneas have been spared from the Plague, though a part of the Greymane Wall now known as [[Oldrock Pass]] was briefly breached by a Scourge warhost led by the lich [[Naze the Eternal]] two years prior to the opening of the Greymane Wall, leading to the destruction of the town of [[Ruins of Greyshire|Greyshire]] and the Scourge being decisively pushed out of Gilneas.<ref>{{questlong|Alliance|42|Scouring Greyshire}}</ref> In the midst of the [[Gilnean civil war]], the Greymane Wall was taken over and opened by the [[Ravenwood Rebellion]]<ref>{{questlong|Alliance|44|Legacy of Perenolde}}</ref><ref>{{questlong|Alliance|38|The Wall Comes Crashing Down}}</ref>, and many refugees that have escaped the Plague have begun migrating into Gilneas and made camp outside of the wall, establishing the [[Vagrant Encampment]].

